@* The layout of the server-rendered pages that carry their own chrome instead of the authenticated shell: the public
   surface and the welcome setup. It gives them the main landmark the React edition's public routes have, so a keyboard or
   screen reader user can reach the content past the navigation, and it carries the framework's error element the way
   MainLayout does. The navigation and the footer are inside the landmark, as they are in the React edition's public routes,
   and the landmark carries the same id the authenticated shell's main does. *@
@inherits LayoutComponentBase

<main id="main-content">@Body</main>

<FrameworkErrorUi/>
